Script returns a tool function and an object holding one (not serializable as data).
-- script.js --
const r = mcp.search_memories({q: "z"});
console.log("hits", r.hits.length);
return {fn: mcp.search_memories, hits: r.hits, arrow: x => x + 1};
-- tools.json --
{
  "search_memories": {
    "hits": [
      {
        "id": "m1"
      }
    ]
  }
}
-- divergence --
Functions inside a returned value: Goja's Export cannot be JSON-encoded (Ditto then returns a %v dump with pointer addresses, which no engine can reproduce); the native engine encodes them as null like JSON.stringify would. Same as adversarial/arr_nested_undefined_export.
